  "label": "audience description",
  "description": "The target community is individuals engaged in political discourse or policy debates, particularly those interested in or affected by abortion law and gun control law. The meme uses political rhetoric to appeal to viewers who may be influenced by simplified arguments and false equivalences, often found in conservative or anti-abortion advocacy circles. The use of a public figure as a speaker lends authority to the argument, targeting audiences who value perceived expert or official opinions. The meme’s harmful intent and misinformation are directed at shaping public opinion on contentious social issues, making it especially relevant to communities involved in legislative or public policy discussions.",
